course: dictionary
lesson: 12165
title: Keeping your composure
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Composure is a noun. It means being calm and in control of your feelings, especially when a moment is difficult or stressful. «Mia kept her composure when the lights went out on stage.» Mia did not panic. She stayed calm, so composure means calm and in control.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Tom lost his composure and cried when his bike crashed.» Crying shows that Tom was upset and not in control of his feelings. So losing composure means stopping being calm when things are hard.
explain: You can also get your composure back. «After a few deep breaths, Sam regained his composure.» Regained means got back again, so Sam became calm once more. Try the swap test: put "calm and in control" into the sentence. Does it still make sense? If yes, you have found the meaning.
fact: Composure means being calm and in control of your feelings.
fact: Composure is often used when someone is under pressure, such as in a race, a game or a test.
fact: Useful phrases: keep your composure, lose your composure, regain composure.
fact: Composure is an uncountable noun, so we say «great composure», not «a composure».
fact: Story writers use composure to show how calm a character is.
exercise: «Mia kept her composure when the lights went out on stage.» What does composure mean here? | Shouting for help | Forgetting her lines | *Staying calm and in control | Running off the stage
exercise: Which phrase shows someone became upset and stopped being calm? | Count your coins | Find your composure again | Keep your composure | *Lose your composure
exercise: «After a few deep breaths, Sam regained his composure.» Find and copy the word that means got back. | Sam | breaths | *regained | deep
test: «Even when the ball hit the post, the goalkeeper kept her composure.» What does this tell us about her? | *She stayed calm and in control | She was angry and threw the ball | She was too tired to move | She ran away from the pitch
test: Which sentence shows someone regaining composure? | Ava ran home without her shoes. | Ava lost her composure and shouted at the teacher. | Ava dropped her bag and laughed loudly. | *After crying, Ava took a breath and became calm again.
exam: Jayden says «composure» means being loud and brave. What does composure really mean? | Being loud and brave | Being alone | *Being calm and in control of your feelings | Being very tired
